  "content": {
    "id": "p3-q13-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "13",
    "prompt": "A certain quantity $x$ is being divided into $n$ equal parts, and also into $n+1$ equal parts. The product of the $n$ parts is $n$ times the product of the $n+1$ parts. Find $x$ in terms of $n$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$x=\\left(\\dfrac{n+1}{n}\\right)^{n+1}$.\n\nExpress each product as a power, then cancel the common factor $x^n$.",
      "worked": "Each of the $n$ parts is $\\dfrac{x}{n}$, and each of the $n+1$ parts is $\\dfrac{x}{n+1}$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\left(\\frac{x}{n}\\right)^n&=n\\left(\\frac{x}{n+1}\\right)^{n+1}\\\\\\frac{x^n}{n^n}&=\\frac{nx^{n+1}}{(n+1)^{n+1}}\\\\\\frac{1}{n^n}&=\\frac{nx}{(n+1)^{n+1}}\\\\x&=\\frac{(n+1)^{n+1}}{n^{n+1}}\\\\x&=\\left(\\frac{n+1}{n}\\right)^{n+1}.\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 58
  },
